1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,410
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds…)

2
00:00:01,410 --> 00:00:02,410
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:03,410
(Also, children and animals were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:05,310
(Episode 4)

5
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:06,380
(Gipyeong Rest Stop)

6
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,480
(2026 Durumi Electronics
Sales Team Workshop)

7
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:14,350
(2026 Durumi Electronics
Sales Team Workshop)

8
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:17,520
Oh, dear.

9
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:19,990
Manager Lee. I'll have a latte.

10
00:00:19,990 --> 00:00:22,030
- Yes. I need to use the restroom.
- Gosh, it hurts.

11
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,060
Okay, go ahead.

12
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:27,970
Team Leader Han.

13
00:00:28,830 --> 00:00:31,200
Well, I wonder if you remember.

14
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:33,710
We made a drinking bet yesterday.

15
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:37,340
The first one to pass out
had to buy snacks at the rest stop.

16
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,180
- Team Leader Bong.
- Yes?

17
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:40,450
Team Leader Bong.

18
00:00:41,980 --> 00:00:42,980
Here you go.

19
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,050
Gosh, thank you, Team Leader Han.

20
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:48,790
I'll try not to go too wild with this.

21
00:00:49,090 --> 00:00:53,260
No, no. Go all out. Go big. Real big.

22
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:55,460
All right. I'll really go for it.

23
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,900
Guys! Let's eat.

24
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,270
What's going on?

25
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,470
Why does that guy scare me?

26
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,200
What?

27
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,030
Did I dream yesterday?

28
00:01:36,630 --> 00:01:37,700
Gosh, my stomach hurts.

29
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:41,370
Why am I so sore and stiff?

30
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:44,140
Oh, my neck.

31
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:47,380
- Manager Yu.
- Yes?

32
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:48,710
Here, drink this. It'll help.

33
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:50,980
A hangover cure?

34
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,690
I don't have a hangover. You drink it.

35
00:01:54,790 --> 00:01:57,620
- I see. You don't have a hangover.
- No.

36
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,160
You were so cool yesterday, Manager Yu.

37
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,900
Why? Did something happen yesterday?

38
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:06,660
It was nothing.

39
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:12,540
Oh, right. You did well.

40
00:02:14,110 --> 00:02:16,440
It was your first time in the field,
so it must've been chaotic, right?

41
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:19,340
You did a good job.

42
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:21,980
Thank you.

43
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:27,420
Manager Yu.
There's one thing I'm curious about.

44
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:28,720
What is it?

45
00:02:28,790 --> 00:02:30,620
Why did you deal with those bastards
like that yesterday?

46
00:02:30,690 --> 00:02:31,820
Differently from the other Meetings?

47
00:02:32,920 --> 00:02:35,530
Didn't you hear?
It was a preliminary Meeting.

48
00:02:43,940 --> 00:02:45,300
It hurts so much.

49
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:48,510
It hurts so bad...

50
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,950
My back.

51
00:02:57,950 --> 00:02:59,050
Darn it.

52
00:03:04,060 --> 00:03:05,120
Sir.

53
00:03:06,390 --> 00:03:07,430
They turned themselves in?

54
00:03:07,490 --> 00:03:10,230
Right at dawn,
a call came into the station.

55
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:12,330
This old man, saying he wanted to confess.

56
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:15,130
He confessed to everything
without even being asked.

57
00:03:15,370 --> 00:03:18,040
He buried all seven of the missing people
after removing their organs.

58
00:03:18,670 --> 00:03:20,040
He was even kind enough
to give us the location.

59
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:22,010
He said he did it
in that warehouse over there.

60
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:24,480
The forensics team
is collecting DNA samples now.

61
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:27,680
But why is everyone in this condition?

62
00:03:27,810 --> 00:03:30,480
They claim they got into
a fight amongst themselves.

63
00:03:31,450 --> 00:03:32,680
To the point they ended up like this?

64
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:36,920
They won't say what they fought over,
so we don't know. But that's their story.

65
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,940
What about recent guests?

66
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:00,980
They haven't been in business
for the past month,

67
00:04:01,350 --> 00:04:03,650
so there were no guests.
Naturally, there's no guest list either.

68
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:07,190
- Have you checked the CCTV?
- About that...

69
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:09,050
The strange thing is...

70
00:04:09,990 --> 00:04:11,060
There's nothing. Not a single thing.

71
00:04:11,620 --> 00:04:13,760
What do you mean? Was it erased?

72
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:15,790
Well, according to them,
it was turned off.

73
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:17,460
So we don't know if it was erased...

74
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:19,000
or if it never recorded anything
to begin with.

75
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:21,000
In my 15 years as a detective,

76
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:22,870
this is the first time I've had a case
handed to me on a platter...

77
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:25,570
We have evidence from the scene
and even a confession.

78
00:04:25,970 --> 00:04:27,140
So even without the CCTV footage...

79
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:31,640
But...

80
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:35,910
(Checkpoint, Reduce Speed)

81
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:43,690
Get out of the car.

82
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:46,120
I said, get out.

83
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:49,590
I told you I'm in a hurry.
I have to go now.

84
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,500
I'm responding to an emergency call.

85
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:53,970
I understand. Now show me your ID.

86
00:04:55,330 --> 00:04:58,340
Gosh, you're so diligent.
Please, just let me go.

87
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,940
My gosh. Where do you think you're going?

88
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:02,040
Someone is dying right now.

89
00:05:02,310 --> 00:05:05,180
I have to perform CPR, you get it?
I'm leaving now.

90
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:07,910
I get it. Now show me your ID.

91
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,120
This guy... Get him. Get him.

92
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,720
- Hey, get him. Get him.
- Darn it...

93
00:05:16,090 --> 00:05:17,290
Beom, what's wrong?

94
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,920
An ambulance was heading
to the bed and breakfast,

95
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,990
so we stopped it for inspection,

96
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:22,390
and the man inside suddenly tried to run,
so we got him.

97
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:24,730
- I see.
- He's wearing a doctor's coat.

98
00:05:24,730 --> 00:05:26,260
I think
he's the organ harvesting specialist.

99
00:05:26,730 --> 00:05:28,970
- A specialist?
- Hurry, get your ID out. Now.

100
00:05:29,030 --> 00:05:30,030
Get him. Get him!

101
00:05:31,370 --> 00:05:32,840
- Hurry up. Get it out.
- Okay, okay.

102
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,140
What's his name?

103
00:05:35,470 --> 00:05:36,470
Jo Dong Min?

104
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,380
It's not Jo Dong Min.

105
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,110
It's Jo Dong Man. It's Man.

106
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:46,620
He says it's Jo Dong Man?
Did you check his ID?

107
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:48,650
Mr. Jo is pretty good at what he does.

108
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,560
Our clients are scheduled to arrive
one every hour,

109
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,990
so if you wait on the road
to the bed and breakfast,

110
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:56,230
you can just pick them off one by one.

111
00:05:56,790 --> 00:05:59,000
- Got it.
- My hands are falling asleep.

112
00:06:01,030 --> 00:06:03,800
He said a client is coming every hour,
so maintain the checkpoint.

113
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:16,010
- Who are you flies buzzing around me?
- Flies?

114
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,420
Die, you wench!

115
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,340
On your knees, you bastard.

116
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,610
On your knees, you bastard.

117
00:06:52,880 --> 00:06:54,690
Hey, get up. On your knees.

118
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:58,190
Get on your knees, you bastards. Kneel.

119
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:11,040
If you hand them over to the police,
isn't it just a waste of time?

120
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:13,540
They won't be punished properly anyway.

121
00:07:15,710 --> 00:07:16,770
And how would you know that?

122
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,110
Whether they'll be
properly punished or not.

123
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,750
The police, the law, the courts...

124
00:07:21,810 --> 00:07:24,050
Do you just blindly distrust
and oppose them?

125
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:27,850
No. It's not necessarily like that.

126
00:07:27,920 --> 00:07:31,120
A preliminary meeting means
we entrust it to the law first.

127
00:07:31,290 --> 00:07:34,190
It means we respect its role
and responsibilities.

128
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:39,030
Of course, there can be limitations.

129
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:43,630
Sometimes a verdict functions
as the minimum punishment,

130
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:47,810
and sometimes, impure things
that shouldn't interfere...

131
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:50,170
get in the way of
rightful punishment by law.

132
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:53,680
But it's not right
to just ignore and cast it aside.

133
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:56,850
We're not trying
to create a lawless world, are we?

134
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:03,590
They do their job, and we do ours.
That's how I see it.

135
00:08:04,990 --> 00:08:08,430
We just sometimes do
the things they can't.

136
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:13,460
Manager Yu.

137
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:21,940
But then again, who knows?

138
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,280
Maybe the day will come when today's...

139
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:26,310
preliminary meeting
becomes an official one.

140
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:30,780
If they forget us.

141
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:40,860
If they forget that somewhere out there,
there are beings scarier than the law.

142
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:48,030
A gang of inhuman organ traffickers...

143
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:52,700
who kidnapped hikers to harvest organs
and bury their bodies...

144
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,340
has been arrested by the police.

145
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:56,540
The victims they kidnapped and murdered...

146
00:08:56,610 --> 00:08:58,310
have all been previously reported
as part of...

147
00:08:58,310 --> 00:09:00,880
the Mount Taegong
serial disappearance case...

148
00:09:01,010 --> 00:09:04,020
and have now been identified
as the missing hikers.

149
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:07,020
(Do Not Enter)

150
00:09:07,690 --> 00:09:08,950
Police announced today...

151
00:09:08,950 --> 00:09:11,390
that they have recovered
the bodies of all the victims...

152
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:14,390
who were secretly buried
in mountains across the country.

153
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:20,630
As for the hospitals that purchased organs
from the traffickers...

154
00:09:20,700 --> 00:09:22,130
and performed illegal surgeries,

155
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,400
they have been raided
and all personnel arrested.

156
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:28,810
Police have obtained
a list of the individuals...

157
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:29,870
who received the illegal transplants...

158
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:32,680
and are expanding the investigation
to the entire medical community.

159
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:37,280
In addition to a full-scale crackdown
on the illegal organ black market,

160
00:09:37,550 --> 00:09:39,280
they believe there are
other medical institutions...

161
00:09:39,350 --> 00:09:40,550
that have committed similar crimes...

162
00:09:40,650 --> 00:09:43,090
and plan to track them down
and punish them severely.

163
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:46,420
Let's hope they remember.

164
00:09:47,860 --> 00:09:51,330
That for those who take
their crimes lightly and scoff at the law,

165
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,660
when they feel most safe and at ease,

166
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:57,770
the harshest punishment of all
will come for them.

167
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:19,020
Oh, I see.
So you're rooting for Kingfisher, then?

168
00:10:19,390 --> 00:10:23,960
Yes, sir, I've noted your expert opinion.
But since we're the police,

169
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:26,460
we have a duty we have to uphold.

170
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:29,970
(Beom Sung Hoon)

171
00:10:30,030 --> 00:10:31,770
Seriously, they said it was a tip,

172
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,540
but they just called to tell us
not to catch Kingfisher.

173
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:35,540
Give me a break.

174
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,540
Tell me about it.

175
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:39,310
Every time a major
violent crime case breaks,

176
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,750
they'd think Kingfisher
was the most precious person in the world.

177
00:10:42,110 --> 00:10:44,650
Gosh. How are we supposed to get
any work done with all this commotion?

178
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:47,450
It'll be 1 or 2 months at most.

179
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:50,290
They're bound to strike
somewhere else soon, right?

180
00:10:52,790 --> 00:10:54,590
- Make sure the chief has his meals.
- Okay.

181
00:10:54,690 --> 00:10:56,130
We're heading out for the stakeout
in Inseong-dong.

182
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:58,160
- Good work.
- We're heading out.

183
00:10:58,160 --> 00:10:59,730
(Violent Crimes Unit 1)

184
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:00,730
Take care out there.

185
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:05,940
Wow, look at the time.

186
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:08,270
Should I order dinner?

187
00:11:09,270 --> 00:11:10,310
The victims.

188
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,240
Sir?

189
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:16,180
When you hit a wall with the perpetrators,
you go after the victims.

190
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:21,620
So far, Kingfisher's pattern has been
from 7 days to 60 days max.

191
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:24,160
Just as Detective Jang said,
they'll strike again somewhere soon.

192
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:29,260
Instead of focusing on a past crime,
what if we go after a future one?

193
00:11:29,990 --> 00:11:31,860
A future crime?

194
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:33,530
Kingfisher's next target.

195
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:35,970
The next target? Who?

196
00:11:40,770 --> 00:11:43,110
- No, I'm not going.
- Why not?

197
00:11:43,710 --> 00:11:46,340
Your daycare is going
to the kids' cafe today.

198
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:49,310
- It'll be so much fun.
- But Mommy's not coming.

199
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:53,280
Yul, Mommy told you she can't
because she has to go to work, right?

200
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:56,490
That's right, Yul. Mommy can't go
because she has to work today.

201
00:11:56,650 --> 00:12:00,060
Instead, Daddy will buy you
new Baby Shark stickers tonight.

202
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:02,130
- How about that?
- No, I don't want them.

203
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,860
This isn't working.
Honey, you go on ahead.

204
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:09,200
You said you have an out-of-town story
and have to leave early. Go.

205
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:10,270
It's still fine.

206
00:12:10,670 --> 00:12:14,610
- We'll get up in a minute. Right, Yul?
- No, I'm not getting up.

207
00:12:14,870 --> 00:12:18,240
Kwon Yul, if you don't get up
by the time I count to five,

208
00:12:18,610 --> 00:12:21,350
I'm going to forcibly get you up
and drag you out of here.

209
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:24,380
- Is that what you want?
- No, don't.

210
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,750
I'm counting.

211
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,080
One.

212
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:28,750
Two...

213
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:31,420
So scary. I think Yul needs to get up now.

214
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:33,190
You know Mommy doesn't play around
when she's mad, right?

215
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:38,100
Three.

216
00:12:38,900 --> 00:12:40,730
Here I come. Four.

217
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:43,930
Mommy doesn't play around.

218
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:51,540
"Doesn't play around."

219
00:12:57,150 --> 00:12:59,250
My daughter is so smart.

220
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:01,420
Give it here.

221
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,920
Right?

222
00:13:03,650 --> 00:13:05,190
Your mom shows no mercy, right?

223
00:13:05,990 --> 00:13:09,590
Your mom has always been that merciless.

224
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:13,730
I was so scared when I first met your mom.

225
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:18,900
So scary. Let's go, let's go. So scary.

226
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:21,840
(Child On Board)

227
00:13:22,770 --> 00:13:26,540
Yul, what did Mommy tell you to do
at the kids' cafe today?

228
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:31,920
Listen to your teacher,
don't fight with your friends,

229
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:34,450
and be careful not to get hurt. Right?

230
00:13:35,090 --> 00:13:37,420
You have to do that. Got it?

231
00:13:37,690 --> 00:13:40,460
It's Seo Jun. Mommy, it's Seo Jun.

232
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:43,790
- I don't want to.
- No. Sweetie...

233
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:48,470
- I'm not going.
- Mommy's running late. Let's go.

234
00:13:50,270 --> 00:13:52,970
My car went in for repairs yesterday,

235
00:13:56,170 --> 00:13:58,310
and I couldn't get a taxi
for the life of me.

236
00:13:59,010 --> 00:14:01,550
Then he threw a tantrum today,
saying he didn't want to go to daycare.

237
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:03,050
That must have been tough.

238
00:14:03,650 --> 00:14:06,950
They say "terrible fours,"
and that's my son exactly these days.

239
00:14:08,150 --> 00:14:09,820
It's a war every morning.

240
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:12,920
And my commute is already a battle
since my office is so far.

241
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:15,130
My mommy goes to work too.

242
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:16,530
That's right, Yul.

243
00:14:17,290 --> 00:14:18,830
You work too?

244
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:23,370
I was on maternity leave,
and I just went back to work recently.

245
00:14:23,770 --> 00:14:24,840
This is just the beginning for me.

246
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,040
I didn't know.

247
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:29,810
My mommy won't come to the kids' cafe.

248
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:32,640
Yul, right?

249
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:36,110
If you just went back,
it must be really tough for you.

250
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:39,150
Going back to the office
after only looking after your kid...

251
00:14:39,150 --> 00:14:40,380
at home every day,

252
00:14:40,750 --> 00:14:42,390
