a harsher sentence in the first place.

378
00:21:17,310 --> 00:21:21,620
- Exactly. Isn't this totally insane?
- Seriously. If I had my way right now,

379
00:21:21,690 --> 00:21:24,220
I'd call Kingfisher this very second.

380
00:21:24,550 --> 00:21:27,090
But I can't because
I don't have the number.

381
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:29,730
- But I'm so angry.
- What do we do now?

382
00:21:29,930 --> 00:21:32,060
How are we supposed to live
when the world is so terrifying?

383
00:21:32,260 --> 00:21:33,500
I'm so furious right now.

384
00:21:34,630 --> 00:21:36,200
The law really needs to change. It does.

385
00:21:36,270 --> 00:21:37,270
What are we going to do?

386
00:21:37,330 --> 00:21:38,940
I mean, how can we let our kids
play outside...

387
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:39,940
with things like this happening?

388
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:42,010
I can't.

389
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:44,710
As a father raising a daughter,

390
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,910
I felt I had to do something,
so I came out here.

391
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:49,550
I mean, if a monster like that is out
on the streets,

392
00:21:49,610 --> 00:21:51,550
how can anyone feel safe
letting their kids outside?

393
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:54,020
Why should we be the ones living in fear?

394
00:21:54,920 --> 00:21:57,220
Okay, thank you for the interview.

395
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:59,620
- He's coming out.
- He's coming out.

396
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:00,660
He's coming out.

397
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:03,090
Go to hell, you piece of scum.
Give him the death penalty.

398
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:10,400
Just die.

399
00:22:19,810 --> 00:22:21,480
(Building A Better Future
Through Advanced Corrections)

400
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:44,740
That bastard.

401
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:53,380
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir.

402
00:22:59,050 --> 00:23:02,220
