00:28:41,560 --> 00:28:43,690
I mean, why do we have to take
a bastard like him by car...

502
00:28:43,690 --> 00:28:45,400
and politely escort him all the way home?

503
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,700
Especially when we're already
so short-staffed.

504
00:28:48,800 --> 00:28:50,570
I don't even know what I'm doing anymore.

505
00:28:50,630 --> 00:28:53,940
Am I supposed to be watching this bastard
or protecting him? Darn it.

506
00:28:53,940 --> 00:28:55,110
Goodness.

507
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:58,170
What's he doing,
making the crap from scratch?

508
00:28:58,480 --> 00:28:59,480
Why isn't he coming out?

509
00:29:03,750 --> 00:29:04,750
What's this?

510
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:07,750
Darn it, what's going on?

511
00:29:10,620 --> 00:29:11,690
What is it?

512
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:14,420
- Excuse me, sorry.
- What's happening? What is it?

513
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:20,160
Detective Lee, over here.

514
00:29:21,700 --> 00:29:23,270
It says the bastard is outside.

515
00:29:26,170 --> 00:29:27,500
Hey, you think that bastard escaped
through the window?

516
00:29:28,870 --> 00:29:29,870
Hurry, hurry.

517
00:29:30,570 --> 00:29:33,580
(Samneung)

518
00:29:38,680 --> 00:29:40,020
Sir, over there.

519
00:29:40,020 --> 00:29:41,320
(Men's Restroom)

520
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:44,320
Detective Lee, you drive.

521
00:29:44,890 --> 00:29:45,990
- Let's go.
- Okay.

522
00:29:46,190 --> 00:29:47,190
Wait a minute.

523
00:29:53,830 --> 00:29:55,770
- Yes?
- Where's Pyo Gyu Cheol?

524
00:30:01,770 --> 00:30:03,910
Look, he can't have gone far,
so let's hurry and go after him.

525
00:30:03,910 --> 00:30:05,380
- Okay.
- Let's go.

526
00:30:08,510 --> 00:30:09,710
Reporter Koo, get in. Hurry.

527
00:30:10,210 --> 00:30:13,450
- Sir, where are we going?
- I don't know, but...

528
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:15,950
it looks like something's happened
to Pyo Gyu Cheol. Let's just go.

529
00:30:15,950 --> 00:30:18,960
(Not Today)

530
00:30:36,610 --> 00:30:38,040
Filthy bastard. Darn it.

531
00:30:45,380 --> 00:30:47,050
(Men's Restroom)

532
00:31:09,010 --> 00:31:10,870
Sir, welcome.

533
00:31:11,510 --> 00:31:12,610
You did well.

534
00:31:18,550 --> 00:31:21,620
Did Park Hui Dong send you?

535
00:31:22,890 --> 00:31:23,890
Of course.

536
00:31:24,190 --> 00:31:26,720
He's at Samjin Port now.

537
00:31:28,090 --> 00:31:29,330
Name, Park Hui Dong.

538
00:31:29,590 --> 00:31:32,500
A fellow inmate who shared a cell
with Pyo Gyu Cheol.

539
00:31:32,730 --> 00:31:35,000
Park Hui Dong served three years
for producing...

540
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:37,700
and distributing digital pornography,
and was released three months ago.

541
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,670
According to our intel,
after Pyo Gyu Cheol is released,

542
00:31:40,670 --> 00:31:43,310
he'll team up with Park Hui Dong
and illegally leave the country,

543
00:31:43,570 --> 00:31:47,210
where we expect them to set up a base
and start producing child pornography.

544
00:31:47,210 --> 00:31:49,610
Shit. Wow, that's insane.

545
00:31:50,180 --> 00:31:51,410
Let's start with the scenario.

546
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:54,420
The meeting date is
on the day of his release, as expected.

547
00:31:54,650 --> 00:31:56,790
But I think we should
move up the timeline.

548
00:31:56,790 --> 00:31:58,190
Before he goes back
to his old neighborhood.

549
00:31:58,620 --> 00:31:59,690
During his transfer?

550
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:01,420
Well, that could get messy.

551
00:32:01,460 --> 00:32:03,990
His last victim still lives
in that neighborhood.

552
00:32:07,730 --> 00:32:10,600
Samneung Rest Stop is
30 minutes from Jungryeong Prison.

553
00:32:10,730 --> 00:32:12,340
We'll grab him there.

554
00:32:13,040 --> 00:32:14,940
Then, two hours from there
is Mount Jeongan.

555
00:32:14,940 --> 00:32:17,340
There's a small birch forest there.

556
00:32:17,540 --> 00:32:19,780
A place Pyo Gyu Cheol
would absolutely hate.

557
00:32:21,740 --> 00:32:23,410
You have a pollen allergy.

558
00:32:25,350 --> 00:32:27,380
That's why I don't usually go
to the mountains.

559
00:32:29,290 --> 00:32:31,720
In the spring,
you should watch out for birch trees,

560
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:34,020
and in the fall,
you'll need to be careful of ragweed.

561
00:32:34,460 --> 00:32:36,390
I'll prepare the allergy medication.

562
00:32:37,290 --> 00:32:39,060
So he can have a little taste of hell.

563
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:41,000
Okay, okay.

564
00:32:41,630 --> 00:32:43,970
Let's keep it simple.

565
00:32:44,230 --> 00:32:47,000
A guy just released from prison
cuts off his electronic ankle monitor...

566
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,000
and flees into the mountains.

567
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:51,710
On a spring day of all days,
he just happens to pass by a birch forest,

568
00:32:52,110 --> 00:32:55,480
when he has a seizure
from his chronic pollen allergy,

569
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:57,250
and falls to his death from a cliff.

570
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:03,250
Anyway, you've got some darn good friends.

571
00:33:03,420 --> 00:33:05,420
You know, in life,

572
00:33:05,490 --> 00:33:08,690
it's hard to meet people
you click with, right?

573
00:33:12,260 --> 00:33:14,730
Well, let me make one phone call.

574
00:33:17,070 --> 00:33:18,070
To whom?

575
00:33:18,770 --> 00:33:20,440
Oh, that friend of yours?

576
00:33:23,110 --> 00:33:24,640
You're so suspicious.

577
00:33:25,810 --> 00:33:27,240
Here. Go ahead.

578
00:33:35,550 --> 00:33:36,550
(President Park)

579
00:33:49,630 --> 00:33:50,630
(President Park, 010-645-6490)

580
00:33:51,770 --> 00:33:52,800
(Call Blocked)

581
00:33:52,800 --> 00:33:54,070
The number you have dialed
is not available.

582
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:55,270
You will be redirected to voicemail...

583
00:33:58,270 --> 00:33:59,480
(Call Blocked)

584
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:02,040
The number you have dialed
is not available.

585
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:05,310
Honestly.
You've got a lot of time on your hands.

586
00:34:05,520 --> 00:34:07,750
Hey, if you don't trust me,
then don't get in.

587
00:34:08,280 --> 00:34:09,520
Then I'm not going either.

588
00:34:10,250 --> 00:34:11,520
Goodness.

589
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:16,430
I mean, look, President Park paid me
a hefty sum...

590
00:34:16,490 --> 00:34:19,760
and begged and pleaded
that you had to leave today,

591
00:34:19,830 --> 00:34:21,930
so I even canceled my meeting
to come here for this.

592
00:34:21,960 --> 00:34:24,970
And I brought an expert
to take off that ankle monitor for you.

593
00:34:25,030 --> 00:34:26,100
This ankle monitor?

594
00:34:26,470 --> 00:34:29,810
Hey, not just anyone can take that off.
It's a huge pain in the ass.

595
00:34:31,970 --> 00:34:34,080
All right, fine. Then you can just
stand around here dawdling...

596
00:34:34,080 --> 00:34:37,910
and get caught by the cops for all I care.
That's none of my business, you hear?

597
00:34:38,450 --> 00:34:39,520
Another thing.

598
00:34:40,420 --> 00:34:42,520
When the party involved refuses...

599
00:34:42,990 --> 00:34:45,490
You know the fee is absolutely
non-refundable, right?

600
00:34:45,990 --> 00:34:48,020
So damn suspicious. Goodness.

601
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:50,560
Hey, what are you doing?
Get in, get in. Let's go home.

602
00:34:50,690 --> 00:34:51,690
We came here for nothing.

603
00:35:01,970 --> 00:35:05,940
Well, anyway,
you really picked a great day.

604
00:35:06,240 --> 00:35:08,810
This is the perfect weather
for skipping town.

605
00:35:10,510 --> 00:35:12,650
Before we skip town,
let's stop by my old neighborhood.

606
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:17,390
What? If you go to your house now,
there'll be people...

607
00:35:17,450 --> 00:35:19,320
swarming all over the place.

608
00:35:19,490 --> 00:35:22,890
And if you go,
you'll see things you shouldn't, right?

609
00:35:23,660 --> 00:35:24,930
Who said anything about going home?

610
00:35:26,460 --> 00:35:28,870
Oh, then where to?

611
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,970
It's just that before I go
on this long journey,

612
00:35:32,400 --> 00:35:34,370
I should at least see her face once.

613
00:35:36,570 --> 00:35:39,380
I'm curious to see how she's grown...

614
00:35:40,540 --> 00:35:44,950
Well, she was about 8 then,
so if I add about 10-something years...

615
00:35:47,250 --> 00:35:49,420
Wow, she must be all grown up now.

616
00:35:58,730 --> 00:36:00,700
Do you really have to go that far?

617
00:36:15,780 --> 00:36:17,050
Nice work, Manager Tae.

618
00:36:20,950 --> 00:36:22,180
Oh, you look comfortable...

619
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:24,590
Let's switch back.

620
00:36:27,590 --> 00:36:29,630
Gosh, I'm just not suited for big cars.

621
00:36:47,210 --> 00:36:49,250
There's something I've been wondering.

622
00:36:49,280 --> 00:36:51,980
Why do you use such complicated methods,
like faking an accident?

623
00:36:52,110 --> 00:36:54,250
A single shot from Kingfisher
would make it so much easier.

624
00:36:54,550 --> 00:36:55,720
We could do that,

625
00:36:55,790 --> 00:36:57,890
but there are too many variables
for one person to handle.

626
00:36:58,420 --> 00:37:01,690
Especially since we're in charge of White.

627
00:37:03,260 --> 00:37:06,200
White... Why?

628
00:37:08,060 --> 00:37:10,330
Cleanly, painlessly, with a single shot.

629
00:37:10,900 --> 00:37:12,030
That's Senior Bo Na's way.

630
00:37:12,640 --> 00:37:14,340
I already knew that.

631
00:37:14,500 --> 00:37:16,740
One shot, one kill.
Kingfisher's signature.

632
00:37:17,440 --> 00:37:18,440
Do you know why that is?

633
00:37:19,580 --> 00:37:20,680
Because...

634
00:37:22,380 --> 00:37:23,550
Because she's good.

635
00:37:26,050 --> 00:37:27,380
It looks like the driver was drowsy.

636
00:37:27,380 --> 00:37:28,480
(Rest Area For Drowsy Drivers)

637
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:30,190
We need to hurry.

638
00:37:40,200 --> 00:37:41,330
This is the truck.

639
00:37:41,600 --> 00:37:42,600
(Name: Pyo Gyu Cheol. 1973.11.04,
Sex: M, Child Sexual Violence)

640
00:37:44,200 --> 00:37:45,300
Beom, check on top.

641
00:37:45,740 --> 00:37:46,740
Yes, sir.

642
00:37:56,950 --> 00:37:57,950
Police.

643
00:37:58,380 --> 00:37:59,880
Stay where you are.
We need your cooperation.

644
00:38:04,650 --> 00:38:05,660
Darn it.

645
00:38:13,800 --> 00:38:15,430
Gosh, that scared me.

646
00:38:15,900 --> 00:38:17,200
I thought it was a dismembered corpse.

647
00:38:32,420 --> 00:38:33,750
Why go to all this trouble?

648
00:38:34,320 --> 00:38:35,950
They could've just dumped it somewhere.

649
00:38:42,060 --> 00:38:43,660
First, let's request cooperation...

650
00:38:43,660 --> 00:38:45,330
from the highway patrol
and nearby precincts...

651
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:47,160
and set up checkpoints
on the surrounding access roads.

652
00:38:47,300 --> 00:38:49,100
We also need to secure
the rest stop's CCTV footage quickly,

653
00:38:49,470 --> 00:38:51,030
so let's move. We don't have time.

654
00:38:55,540 --> 00:38:56,540
What's this?

655
00:38:57,070 --> 00:38:59,210
Kwon Tae Sung. What are you doing here?

656
00:38:59,480 --> 00:39:01,510
- Reporter Koo, hurry.
- Hey, hold on. Wait.

657
00:39:01,510 --> 00:39:03,080
- Don't let them touch anything.
- Yes, sir.

658
00:39:03,650 --> 00:39:05,280
- Please put the camera away. Put it away.
- Hey, wait. Hold on.

659
00:39:05,280 --> 00:39:06,480
I'm sorry, can I just take one picture?

660
00:39:06,580 --> 00:39:07,750
- I said no.
- Hey.

661
00:39:07,820 --> 00:39:11,250
- Come on, why are you being like this?
- Were you tailing me? From where?

662
00:39:11,390 --> 00:39:13,520
Tailing you?
I happened to see you at the rest stop.

663
00:39:13,520 --> 00:39:15,190
I was on my way back from covering
Pyo Gyu Cheol's release.

664
00:39:16,230 --> 00:39:18,430
You lost Pyo Gyu Cheol, didn't you?

665
00:39:19,330 --> 00:39:20,800
Is this related to Kingfisher?

666
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:22,770
What?

667
00:39:22,970 --> 00:39:24,700
Don't give me that. You're at the scene
where you lost Pyo Gyu Cheol,

668
00:39:24,770 --> 00:39:26,400
and the detective in charge
of the Kingfisher case is here,

669
00:39:26,470 --> 00:39:28,600
even though it's not your jurisdiction.
A detective from Seoul, at that.

670
00:39:30,370 --> 00:39:31,810
Why is this guy's intuition so good?

671
00:39:32,010 --> 00:39:33,480
What is this?

672
00:39:34,440 --> 00:39:35,480
Is it...

673
00:39:37,010 --> 00:39:38,710
I'm just speculating at this point.

674
00:39:39,720 --> 00:39:42,520
I came here thinking he might be
the next target, but we've hit a dead end.

675
00:39:42,550 --> 00:39:44,120
First, we need to find Pyo Gyu Cheol.

676
00:39:44,190 --> 00:39:45,290
Whether he's alive or dead.

677
00:39:46,220 --> 00:39:47,560
You're saying he could be dead?

678
00:39:48,590 --> 00:39:50,790
Don't jump to conclusions.
He could've just fled.

679
00:39:51,530 --> 00:39:53,160
I'm busy, so get going.

680
00:39:53,230 --> 00:39:54,230
Seriously, please don't.

681
00:39:54,530 --> 00:39:56,030
- I'll just take one picture.
- Reporter Kwon Tae Sung.

682
00:39:56,030 --> 00:39:57,330
I'm refusing to comment from now on.

683
00:39:57,770 --> 00:39:58,830
Now, hurry up.

684
00:39:59,540 --> 00:40:00,670
Don't take pictures.

685
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:02,170
- Get this out of here.
- Yes, sir.

686
00:40:06,110 --> 00:40:07,840
The police are on the move.

687
00:40:08,180 --> 00:40:09,810
There's a checkpoint at the tollgate
20km ahead.

688
00:40:13,150 --> 00:40:15,620
- You should get off now.
- Okay.

689
00:40:15,950 --> 00:40:17,820
- Let's take a detour.
- Okay.

690
00:40:22,530 --> 00:40:23,530
Mommy first?

691
00:40:27,900 --> 00:40:29,060
Delicious.

692
00:40:33,670 --> 00:40:36,670
- Is it good, sweetie?
- Yes. It's so, so good.

693
00:40:37,070 --> 00:40:38,810
- Is it yummy?
- Yes.

694
00:40:38,870 --> 00:40:40,780
My Yul is in a great mood today.

695
00:40:41,340 --> 00:40:42,410
Were you happy that Mommy came?

696
00:40:42,410 --> 00:40:44,080
Yes. I was so, so happy.

697
00:40:45,550 --> 00:40:48,850
Then maybe Mommy shouldn't go to work
and stay by Yul's side every day. Right?

698
00:40:50,390 --> 00:40:51,820
No, Mommy, go to work.

699
00:40:52,120 --> 00:40:54,590
What? You want me to work? Why?

700
00:40:55,060 --> 00:40:56,330
It's necessary work.

701
00:40:58,260 --> 00:40:59,260
What?

702
00:41:02,730 --> 00:41:05,430
Dad said he's not done
with his work at the office yet.

703
00:41:05,530 --> 00:41:07,470
- Want me to sing you a song?
- What kind of work?

704
00:41:08,740 --> 00:41:09,870
Your dad...

705
00:41:09,940 --> 00:41:12,210
Well, a very, very important job.

706
00:41:12,640 --> 00:41:17,080
Your dad is a wonderful person
who does great things for people.

707
00:41:17,250 --> 00:41:18,350
What about you?

708
00:41:18,550 --> 00:41:19,550
What?

709
00:41:19,820 --> 00:41:21,280
What kind of work do you do?

710
00:41:23,790 --> 00:41:27,090
I do... Well...

711
00:41:31,260 --> 00:41:32,260
Necessary work.

712
00:41:32,330 --> 00:41:33,400
Necessary work?

713
00:41:35,130 --> 00:41:36,130
Yes.

714
00:41:38,430 --> 00:41:39,800
Work the world needs.

715
00:41:44,370 --> 00:41:46,280
Oh, you're such a smart girl.

716
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:09,230
(Pilhyeon 2-ri, Pilhyeon 1-ri)

717
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:21,340
(Baby On Board)

718
00:43:04,990 --> 00:43:05,990
We shouldn't have come.

719
00:43:21,500 --> 00:43:23,340
What's going on, sir?

720
00:43:48,330 --> 00:43:50,230
Go, go. Quickly.

721
00:43:55,600 --> 00:43:56,610
What?

722
00:43:58,970 --> 00:44:00,210
Sir, are you okay?

723
00:44:07,680 --> 00:44:08,780
Sir, are you okay?

724
00:44:09,650 --> 00:44:10,650
I'm fine.

725
00:44:11,290 --> 00:44:12,290
That Pyo Gyu Cheol...

726
00:44:12,390 --> 00:44:14,320
We're going to have to hold off
because of the witness.

727
00:44:14,690 --> 00:44:15,820
Get Pyo Gyu Cheol now.

728
00:44:16,260 --> 00:44:17,760
- Get him.
- Yes, sir.

729
00:44:17,860 --> 00:44:20,730
Sir, the bleeding won't stop. Your wound.

730
00:44:20,960 --> 00:44:22,870
- Darn it.
- What do we do?

731
00:44:28,400 --> 00:44:29,570
I said stop the car. Stop.

732
00:44:33,940 --> 00:44:37,110
Oh, Dong Hoon, no. Dong Hoon!

733
00:44:37,410 --> 00:44:40,720
- Dong Hoon. Dong Hoon.
- I'm Pyo Gyu Cheol, you bastards.

734
00:44:42,620 --> 00:44:44,990
Who the hell sent you to kill me?

735
00:44:45,590 --> 00:44:47,790
Hey, they're all still alive and well.

736
00:44:48,220 --> 00:44:50,860
So why are you making such a big deal?
You worthless scum.

737
00:44:53,630 --> 00:44:56,300
- Mom...
- Who the hell is this kid?

738
00:44:57,030 --> 00:44:58,100
Mom.

739
00:45:00,040 --> 00:45:02,040
Dong Hoon.

740
00:45:04,540 --> 00:45:05,670
- Sir.
- Yes?

741
00:45:05,770 --> 00:45:06,840
Are you okay to drive?

742
00:45:09,980 --> 00:45:11,150
Yes, I'm still okay.

743
00:45:11,680 --> 00:45:12,920
Did you find Pyo Gyu Cheol?

744
00:45:14,550 --> 00:45:15,880
Those bastards. Darn it.

745
00:45:18,520 --> 00:45:20,290
This bastard hasn't been
answering his phone.

746
00:45:20,290 --> 00:45:21,690
Answer the phone, darn it.

747
00:45:25,430 --> 00:45:26,500
What's this now?

748
00:45:30,070 --> 00:45:31,470
That moron.

749
00:45:32,400 --> 00:45:33,400
He didn't get far.

750
00:45:34,100 --> 00:45:35,270
Can you confirm the GPS location?

751
00:45:36,340 --> 00:45:37,340
Yes, I can.

752
00:45:40,640 --> 00:45:41,980
It looks like he's heading toward Incheon.

753
00:45:42,640 --> 00:45:43,780
I think he's trying to get on a boat.

754
00:45:45,110 --> 00:45:47,980
- What's this?
- What now? Come on, what is it?

755
00:45:49,790 --> 00:45:51,390
Gosh, that bastard. Darn it.

756
00:45:53,620 --> 00:45:55,360
Mom, I want some gummies. Gummies.

757
00:45:55,390 --> 00:45:58,960
What? Yul, sweetie,
if you eat too much of that,

758
00:45:59,030 --> 00:46:02,700
the doctor said
sugar bugs will grow in your mouth.

759
00:46:02,760 --> 00:46:04,000
Then we'll have to go
to the dentist again.

760
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:05,070
Would you be okay with that?

761
00:46:05,330 --> 00:46:06,970
- I don't want to.
- You don't, right?

762
00:46:07,570 --> 00:46:11,110
Then how about we have
some grilled fish today?

763
00:46:11,170 --> 00:46:13,840
- How about some mackerel? You love that.
- I love mackerel.

764
00:46:13,980 --> 00:46:15,410
- Yul, this mackerel...
- This is breaking news.

765
00:46:15,410 --> 00:46:17,810
After a 16-year prison sentence,

766
00:46:17,810 --> 00:46:19,920
child sex offender Pyo Gyu Cheol,
who was released today,

767
00:46:19,980 --> 00:46:23,750
has cut off his electronic ankle monitor
and escaped while being transported.

768
00:46:24,290 --> 00:46:26,050
The police have issued an emergency alert,

769
00:46:26,120 --> 00:46:28,460
and they are focusing all efforts
on his capture.

770
00:46:28,520 --> 00:46:31,630
Pyo has reportedly carjacked
a passing vehicle and fleeing...

771
00:46:31,630 --> 00:46:34,460
- with a three-year-old hostage.
- Got the mackerel. Should we go?

772
00:46:34,860 --> 00:46:38,500
Police believe Pyo used the cell phone
of the vehicle's owner,

773
00:46:38,500 --> 00:46:39,500
and there's evidence he tried to call.

774
00:46:39,500 --> 00:46:41,340
The police told us to come here.

775
00:46:41,370 --> 00:46:42,470
Is the child safe?

776
00:46:42,470 --> 00:46:45,070
Can you at least tell us
the parole officers' current location?

777
00:46:45,070 --> 00:46:46,140
We don't have that information.

778
00:46:46,210 --> 00:46:47,340
- You're right here.
- Why won't you say anything?

779
00:46:47,340 --> 00:46:48,880
- Please just confirm it.
- I'm sorry.

780
00:46:53,650 --> 00:46:55,120
(Detective Lee Dong Jin)

781
00:46:56,220 --> 00:46:59,090
Tae Sung,
we're not getting anything over here.

782
00:47:00,660 --> 00:47:02,820
That bastard. If he was going to run,

783
00:47:02,820 --> 00:47:04,660
he should've gone alone.
Why take a child...

784
00:47:04,830 --> 00:47:06,900
I'll get an update from my contact
on the police beat,

785
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:08,900
so Reporter Koo, why don't you head back
and start on the research?

786
00:47:09,870 --> 00:47:10,870
What?

787
00:47:13,800 --> 00:47:16,270
Mommy.

788
00:47:17,910 --> 00:47:19,640
Darn it. They're relentless.

789
00:47:21,040 --> 00:47:22,180
You all know the drill, right?

790
00:47:23,010 --> 00:47:26,550
The child's safety is our top priority.
So don't get too close...

791
00:47:27,320 --> 00:47:28,350
and don't provoke him.

792
00:47:28,550 --> 00:47:30,290
We wait for the right opportunity
to strike.

793
00:47:30,990 --> 00:47:32,850
- Everyone got that?
- Yes.

794
00:47:34,820 --> 00:47:36,790
Shut up, you little brat. Shut your mouth.

795
00:47:37,460 --> 00:47:39,490
Mommy.

796
00:47:39,960 --> 00:47:41,460
Mommy.

797
00:47:45,730 --> 00:47:46,740
Darn it.

798
00:47:51,910 --> 00:47:54,040
(Baby On Board)

799
00:47:58,680 --> 00:47:59,680
That bastard...

800
00:48:02,350 --> 00:48:03,420
Is he out of his mind?

801
00:48:30,810 --> 00:48:31,810
(Senior Bo Na)

802
00:48:32,910 --> 00:48:33,920
(Senior Bo Na)

803
00:48:42,590 --> 00:48:43,590
Hey, Tae Min.

804
00:48:44,090 --> 00:48:45,360
Go, get that bastard.

805
00:48:51,570 --> 00:48:53,440
Hyun Nam, how's the child?

806
00:48:53,770 --> 00:48:55,170
Thankfully,
he doesn't appear to be injured.

807
00:48:55,300 --> 00:48:56,510
I'll get him in the car first.

808
00:48:57,840 --> 00:48:58,840
You're okay.

809
00:49:00,810 --> 00:49:01,810
Mommy.

810
00:49:07,320 --> 00:49:08,420
(Baekmari)

811
00:49:12,990 --> 00:49:14,120
(Baekmari)

812
00:49:41,180 --> 00:49:43,250
What's wrong? Come on.

813
00:49:44,020 --> 00:49:46,590
Come on, come on.
What are you waiting for?

814
00:49:47,020 --> 00:49:48,020
I said, come on.

815
00:49:49,790 --> 00:49:52,630
You bastards.
You think I'm some kind of joke?

816
00:49:52,990 --> 00:49:54,000
Go ahead, kill me.

817
00:49:54,200 --> 00:49:55,260
I said, kill me.

818
00:49:55,930 --> 00:49:58,330
Go on, kill me, you bastards.

819
00:49:59,900 --> 00:50:01,770
I'm out of here.

820
00:50:28,730 --> 00:50:29,730
Meeting's over.

821
00:50:29,730 --> 00:50:30,730
(Baekmari)

822
00:50:45,710 --> 00:50:48,780
Actually, Senior Bo Na
doesn't like the sight of blood.

823
00:50:49,620 --> 00:50:51,790
She hates watching someone die...

824
00:50:51,790 --> 00:50:53,620
in front of her in pain.

825
00:50:54,420 --> 00:50:55,790
That's why she prefers sniping.

826
00:50:56,760 --> 00:50:59,930
She doesn't have to
confront them up close,

827
00:51:00,630 --> 00:51:03,700
and she avoids using
unnecessarily cruel violence...

828
00:51:03,770 --> 00:51:05,570
or inflicting pain.

829
00:51:06,800 --> 00:51:10,140
It's purely for the objective of
making them disappear from this world.

830
00:51:11,570 --> 00:51:12,640
White is up.

831
00:51:15,880 --> 00:51:18,780
But there was an exception
for those who hurt children.

832
00:51:19,750 --> 00:51:22,480
That's why the other team members
handled those cases until now.

833
00:51:23,350 --> 00:51:24,350
I don't know.

834
00:51:24,650 --> 00:51:26,690
Maybe she thought it was
too easy a death for them,

835
00:51:27,420 --> 00:51:30,660
or maybe there was another reason.

836
00:51:38,870 --> 00:51:39,870
Anyway, today,

837
00:51:41,940 --> 00:51:43,640
Senior Bo Na ended up
being the one to finish it.

838
00:52:03,190 --> 00:52:04,530
(Not Today)

839
00:52:04,530 --> 00:52:06,190
They're all dead? How?

840
00:52:06,930 --> 00:52:10,530
A car accident, a fall, a drowning.

841
00:52:11,130 --> 00:52:12,300
Another car accident?

842
00:52:12,700 --> 00:52:14,140
Gosh, and even an electrocution.

843
00:52:14,970 --> 00:52:16,240
And what's weird is,

844
00:52:16,610 --> 00:52:19,240
they all died on the day
they were released from prison.

845
00:52:21,710 --> 00:52:23,080
Don't you think that's strange?

846
00:52:24,080 --> 00:52:26,580
If they were shot by Kingfisher,
that'd be one thing,

847
00:52:27,080 --> 00:52:28,550
but how could
every single one of them die...

848
00:52:28,550 --> 00:52:30,420
a violent death
on the day of their release?

849
00:52:34,160 --> 00:52:36,320
- Call 911, now.
- Okay, okay.

850
00:52:36,560 --> 00:52:40,000
Just bad luck, right?
We have to call it a freak accident.

851
00:52:40,560 --> 00:52:41,760
He was such a vicious bastard.

852
00:52:41,760 --> 00:52:43,630
Honestly, even if he had been shot
and killed by Kingfisher,

853
00:52:43,700 --> 00:52:44,830
it wouldn't have been strange at all.

854
00:52:46,230 --> 00:52:48,700
(Choi Il Hwan (Police Reporter))

855
00:52:49,370 --> 00:52:51,070
Choi, how did it go? On the police side...

856
00:52:52,010 --> 00:52:53,210
- We have breaking news. Pyo Gyu Cheol,
- What?

857
00:52:53,210 --> 00:52:55,180
- who cut his ankle monitor and fled...
- Tae Sung, Tae Sung!

858
00:52:55,180 --> 00:52:56,710
- after release today,
- Look at the news.

859
00:52:56,850 --> 00:52:59,580
has been found dead after being shot
with a sniper rifle.

860
00:52:59,810 --> 00:53:02,150
Mr. Pyo abandoned the stolen vehicle...

861
00:53:02,220 --> 00:53:05,150
and was attempting to escape
on a fishing boat docked nearby...

862
00:53:05,390 --> 00:53:07,660
when he was shot in the head
and fell into the ocean.

863
00:53:07,720 --> 00:53:09,520
He was later found dead.

864
00:53:10,990 --> 00:53:11,990
A blanket too?

865
00:53:14,230 --> 00:53:16,200
All right, got it.
Please secure this area.

866
00:53:16,200 --> 00:53:17,270
Thank you.

867
00:53:17,400 --> 00:53:18,500
(Paramedics)

868
00:53:19,270 --> 00:53:20,270
Sir.

869
00:53:20,870 --> 00:53:22,670
The child was safely returned
to his parents.

870
00:53:23,070 --> 00:53:25,170
He was found lying on a sofa
in the management office.

871
00:53:25,240 --> 00:53:26,240
He was even covered with a blanket.

872
00:53:26,840 --> 00:53:27,840
That's a relief.

873
00:53:30,250 --> 00:53:32,180
Gosh, what is this?

874
00:53:33,110 --> 00:53:34,950
If this was a sniper
and not an accident...

875
00:53:38,290 --> 00:53:39,420
I really don't know.

876
00:53:41,690 --> 00:53:45,090
I don't know if we're on the right track
or completely barking up the wrong tree.

877
00:53:49,630 --> 00:53:51,600
I feel terrible for Manager Yu.

878
00:53:52,100 --> 00:53:54,440
We should have found a way
to handle it ourselves.

879
00:53:54,800 --> 00:53:57,840
Now we've made her a target
for the police again.

880
00:53:58,810 --> 00:54:02,140
That's right. There's no way to disguise
a sniper attack as an accident.

881
00:54:02,810 --> 00:54:06,480
The bullet is left behind as evidence,
like Kingfisher's signature.

882
00:54:09,450 --> 00:54:11,020
Just a little longer. I'm almost done.

883
00:54:12,450 --> 00:54:13,590
Isn't it ironic?

884
00:54:15,060 --> 00:54:17,860
That bullet puts Manager Yu in danger,
but instead,

885
00:54:18,430 --> 00:54:19,630
it's protecting all of us.

886
00:54:20,060 --> 00:54:21,230
What is that supposed to mean?

887
00:54:21,830 --> 00:54:23,370
She's basically acting as a decoy.

888
00:54:23,930 --> 00:54:25,170
Diverting the investigation to herself.

889
00:54:26,100 --> 00:54:29,500
Because Manager Yu gets all the attention
under the name Kingfisher,

890
00:54:29,570 --> 00:54:31,870
it allows other cases
to be quietly buried.

891
00:54:32,310 --> 00:54:33,580
It was the same with the Musan case.

892
00:54:34,940 --> 00:54:37,480
So Manager Yu is
in the most dangerous position.

893
00:54:38,280 --> 00:54:39,950
And has the highest risk of being caught.

894
00:54:40,850 --> 00:54:41,850
Bingo.

895
00:54:41,920 --> 00:54:45,350
That's why we all feel so sorry for
and grateful to Manager Yu.

896
00:54:45,750 --> 00:54:47,190
But still, besides Manager Yu,

897
00:54:48,420 --> 00:54:49,760
there's no one else who can do this job.

898
00:54:50,790 --> 00:54:52,330
She's the best one we've got.

899
00:54:54,160 --> 00:54:55,160
I'm all done.

900
00:54:56,560 --> 00:54:57,570
Good work.

901
00:55:03,670 --> 00:55:04,770
Here you go.

902
00:55:06,140 --> 00:55:08,780
My, what's all this...

903
00:55:08,840 --> 00:55:11,710
You really don't have to do this
for me every time.

904
00:55:12,410 --> 00:55:14,080
You rushed all the way over here
from the library...

905
00:55:14,150 --> 00:55:15,320
where you were writing your thesis.

906
00:55:16,020 --> 00:55:19,420
- I feel especially bad today.
- To be honest, I was just dozing off.

907
00:55:19,590 --> 00:55:22,120
- Oh, come on.
- Did you get everything taken care of?

908
00:55:22,620 --> 00:55:24,690
I heard a Client filed a complaint
last minute.

909
00:55:25,130 --> 00:55:27,430
Thanks to you, yes. It's all sorted out.

910
00:55:27,960 --> 00:55:29,730
- Thank you.
- Mommy.

911
00:55:30,600 --> 00:55:31,700
Yul, sweetie, are you awake?

912
00:55:32,330 --> 00:55:33,970
Yul. Oh, sweetie.

913
00:55:33,970 --> 00:55:37,510
She seemed a little gloomy,
and the next thing I knew, she was asleep.

914
00:55:37,970 --> 00:55:39,740
Really? You were?

915
00:55:40,440 --> 00:55:42,810
Yul, I'm so sorry I had to leave
when I promised I'd stay with you today.

916
00:55:44,880 --> 00:55:46,550
Then just give me lots of hugs.

917
00:55:48,350 --> 00:55:50,250
Okay, then I'll give you
lots and lots of hugs.

918
00:55:50,320 --> 00:55:51,690
You give Mommy a hug too.

919
00:55:55,090 --> 00:55:57,360
How's that, Yul?
Feeling a little better now?

920
00:55:57,560 --> 00:55:58,860
Yes, I'm better.

921
00:55:59,330 --> 00:56:00,330
What about you, Mommy?

922
00:56:01,860 --> 00:56:02,860
Me?

923
00:56:05,070 --> 00:56:06,070
I'm okay too.

924
00:56:08,200 --> 00:56:10,840
When I'm holding you like this,
everything's all right.

925
00:56:25,320 --> 00:56:27,460
A sniper this time?

926
00:56:28,090 --> 00:56:29,190
Again? On the day of his release?

927
00:56:29,960 --> 00:56:31,630
Tae Sung, what is this?

928
00:56:33,760 --> 00:56:36,930
I think this has something to do
with Kingfisher.

929
00:56:37,330 --> 00:56:38,470
Shouldn't we look into this?

930
00:57:07,600 --> 00:57:09,700
The return address on this
says it's from Russia.

931
00:57:10,670 --> 00:57:11,930
It's from a friend.

932
00:57:12,870 --> 00:57:17,440
Yul, look.
Your mom's friend sent you a doll.

933
00:57:17,770 --> 00:57:19,640
- You're so lucky, Yul.
- It's mine.

934
00:57:20,440 --> 00:57:22,240
- Mommy, give it to me.
- Okay, here you go.

935
00:57:23,680 --> 00:57:24,950
It's mine.

936
00:57:26,010 --> 00:57:27,020
So cute.

937
00:57:31,520 --> 00:57:35,220
So these are Russian letters.
What does it say?

938
00:57:36,490 --> 00:57:37,490
It's just a friendly note.

939
00:57:37,660 --> 00:57:39,490
You know, "How are you?"
"Miss you," that kind of thing.

940
00:57:41,160 --> 00:57:42,700
That's nice.

941
00:57:42,800 --> 00:57:45,130
You even have friends
who send you gifts from overseas.

942
00:57:45,800 --> 00:57:47,270
I guess so. It's nice to have friends.

943
00:58:52,070 --> 00:58:55,140
(You're good at keeping promises. Good.
Good night again tonight, Tae Sung)

944
00:59:07,920 --> 00:59:09,180
(You're good at keeping promises. Good.
Good night again tonight, Tae Sung)

945
00:59:44,550 --> 00:59:47,390
(A Bona Fide Killer)

946
00:59:47,460 --> 00:59:49,160
Without me knowing, when did our home...

947
00:59:49,290 --> 00:59:52,290
- get a new family member?
- A gift came from Russia.

948
00:59:52,330 --> 00:59:53,760
They said they're coming to Korea soon.

949
00:59:54,730 --> 00:59:57,170
He's the troublemaker youngest son
of the Royal Family.

950
00:59:57,500 --> 00:59:58,870
Seriously, why did you have to act up?

951
00:59:58,930 --> 01:00:01,200
We need to find out now
if it was just an accident...

952
01:00:01,300 --> 01:00:03,970
or a wrongful death disguised as one.

953
01:00:04,070 --> 01:00:06,170
Either way, Chairman Cheon Seong Gyu
is at the center of it.

954
01:00:06,270 --> 01:00:08,480
This seems to be a complex and tangled...

955
01:00:08,580 --> 01:00:10,010
and terrifying case.

956
01:00:10,210 --> 01:00:13,410
Kingfisher's M.O. isn't
limited to just sniping.

957
01:00:13,720 --> 01:00:16,050
- A joint investigation?
- I'll take care of it.

958
01:00:16,180 --> 01:00:18,020
It's too dangerous for you
to be exposed in the field.

959
01:00:18,620 --> 01:00:19,620
Mother.

960
01:00:19,620 --> 01:00:22,020
This is our family's rite, but you make
your daughter-in-law do all the work?

961
01:00:22,020 --> 01:00:23,420
I don't think that's fair.

962
01:00:23,520 --> 01:00:24,530
You little brat.

963
01:00:24,590 --> 01:00:26,130
- Goodness.
- Seriously!

964
01:00:26,560 --> 01:00:28,430
Yul... Yul is missing.

965
01:00:34,200 --> 01:00:36,200
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
